Z||000004||TheFiero64||09-05-2000||05:27 PM||||Great I just spent $530 bucks for tires. I would probably screw up the painting of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Seeing how they are mint and will look great on my 86 GT w/ Silver ground effects when I get an engine in it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jaygee79||09-05-2000||08:22 PM||||The picture doesn't do it justice.  They actually look really good in person.  I found a few others online that had the same thing.  Besides, if you're saving them for the GT, then definitely don't paint them, you'll only have to paint them grey again later on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||09-05-2000||11:10 PM||||Actually going to black isn't that hard if the rest of the wheels are in good shape. Just tape off the bare aluminum areas and the tires then spray Permatex Gasket remover on the grey areas. Once stripped and clean paint them black. ||||reg||1
